\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{States and conditional expectations}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Can the physics be rebuilt from its observables alone? This chapter asks how
a state on a finite-dimensional algebra determines a Hilbert space.}

\p{The first section builds that space from the Gram form #{\omega(a^*b)}.
Its dimension is the rank of the Gram matrix. On a direct sum of matrix
algebras that rank is the sum of each block size times the rank of the
density, and on functions the space is #{\ell^2} of the support. No norm
on the algebra is assumed.}

\p{A Wick conditional expectation sends polynomials to polynomials in the
retained variables, and nested retained sets compose. The normalized
Grassmann state of an invertible paired precision restricts to the
state of the Schur complement. When a residual integral is divided by
the weight of the eliminated variables, does one direct elimination
equal the same elimination performed in successive steps?}

